1
00:04:20,689 --> 00:04:26,689
Heroes aren't born. They're built.

2
00:08:41,379 --> 00:08:47,379
Iron Man is a action, science fiction, adventure film directed by Jon Favreau.

3
00:13:02,068 --> 00:13:08,068
After being held captive in an Afghan cave, billionaire engineer Tony Stark
creates a unique weaponized suit of armor to fight evil.

4
00:17:22,758 --> 00:17:28,758
Tony Stark, played by Robert Downey Jr..

5
00:21:43,448 --> 00:21:49,448
Rhodey, played by Terrence Howard.

6
00:26:04,137 --> 00:26:10,137
Obadiah Stane, played by Jeff Bridges.

7
00:30:24,827 --> 00:30:30,827
Pepper Potts, played by Gwyneth Paltrow.

8
00:34:45,517 --> 00:34:51,517
Christine Everhart, played by Leslie Bibb.

9
00:39:06,206 --> 00:39:12,206
Yinsen, played by Shaun Toub.

10
00:43:26,896 --> 00:43:32,896
Iron Man is a 2008 American superhero film based on the
Marvel Comics character of the same name.

11
00:47:47,586 --> 00:47:53,586
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Paramount Pictures, it is
the first film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

12
00:52:08,275 --> 00:52:14,275
Directed by Jon Favreau from a screenplay by the writing teams of Mark Fergus and Hawk
Ostby, and Art Marcum and Matt Holloway, the film stars Robert Downey Jr.

13
00:56:28,965 --> 00:56:34,965
as Tony Stark / Iron Man alongside Terrence Howard, Jeff
Bridges, Gwyneth Paltrow, Leslie Bibb, and Shaun Toub.

14
01:00:49,655 --> 01:00:55,655
In the film, following his escape from captivity by a terrorist group, world-famous industrialist and
master engineer Stark builds a mechanized suit of armor and becomes the superhero Iron Man.

15
01:05:10,344 --> 01:05:16,344
A film featuring Iron Man was in development at Universal Pictures, 20th Century Fox, and New Line
Cinema at various times since 1990 before Marvel Studios reacquired the rights in 2005.

16
01:09:31,034 --> 01:09:37,034
Marvel put the project in production as its first
self-financed film, with Paramount Pictures distributing.

17
01:13:51,724 --> 01:13:57,724
Favreau signed on as director in April 2006 and faced opposition from Marvel when
trying to cast Downey in the title role; the actor was signed in September.

18
01:18:12,413 --> 01:18:18,413
Filming took place from March to June 2007, primarily in California to differentiate the
film from numerous other superhero stories that are set in New York City.

19
01:22:33,103 --> 01:22:39,103
During filming, the actors were free to create their own dialogue
because pre-production was focused on the story and action.

20
01:26:53,793 --> 01:26:59,793
Rubber and metal versions of the armor, created by Stan Winston's company, were
mixed with computer-generated imagery to create the title character.

21
01:31:14,482 --> 01:31:20,482
Iron Man premiered in Sydney on April 14, 2008, and was released in the United
States on May 2, as the first film in Phase One of the MCU.

22
01:35:35,172 --> 01:35:41,172
It grossed over $585 million, becoming the eighth-highest grossing film of 2008, and received praise from critics, especially
for Downey's performance as well as Favreau's direction, the visual effects, action sequences, and writing.

23
01:39:55,862 --> 01:40:01,862
The American Film Institute selected it as one of the ten best films of 2008.

24
01:44:16,551 --> 01:44:22,551
It received two nominations at the 81st Academy Awards for
Best Sound Editing and Best Visual Effects.

25
01:48:37,241 --> 01:48:43,241
In 2022, the Library of Congress selected the film for preservation in the United States National
Film Registry for being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

26
01:52:57,931 --> 01:53:03,931
Two sequels have been released: Iron Man 2 (2010) and Iron Man 3 (2013).

27
01:57:18,620 --> 01:57:24,620
The film explores themes of middle east, superhero,
arms dealer, malibu, based on comic.

28
02:01:39,310 --> 02:01:45,310
The tone is thought_provoking.
